2026-02-13  Kamila Szewczyk  <k@iczelia.net>

	* Version 0.0.4 released.

	* .github/workflows/ci.yml: Replace run-on-arch-action with Docker
	QEMU emulation for exotic architectures. Add new CI targets: ppc64
	(big-endian), powerpc (32-bit), hppa (HP PA-RISC), m68k (Motorola
	68000), sh4 (Hitachi SuperH), alpha (DEC Alpha), mips64le, arm32v7,
	arm32v5. All exotic architectures build without LTO due to toolchain
	limitations. Use debian-ports images for ppc64/powerpc/hppa/m68k/sh4/
	alpha via urbanogilson/debian-debootstrap-ports.
	Ensure file(1) is installed in exotic Docker jobs so libtool can
	detect mips64 linker emulation correctly (avoid invalid "-m elf").

	* .github/workflows/release.yml: Update release notes template with
	all supported architecture tuples including new exotic targets.
	Bundle binary artifacts into c-arbint-<version>-bin.tar.xz,
	c-arbint-<version>-bin.tar.bz3, and c-arbint-<version>-bin.zip
	instead of uploading each libarbint-* file individually.

	* tests/run_wasm_test.sh: Pass through extra command-line arguments
	to wasm test binaries (e.g., --test flag for dc demo).

	* demos/Makefile.am: Add dc_LOG_FLAGS = --test to run dc demo in
	automated test mode instead of interactive mode.

	* src/arbint_str.c, src/arbint_str.h: New files. Implement string
	conversion functions arbint_set_str and arbint_get_str. Supports
	bases 2-62 with case-insensitive parsing for bases 2-36 and
	case-sensitive for 37-62. Uses fast divide-and-conquer algorithm
	for large numbers: recursively splits number at B^(n/2) and
	converts halves independently, achieving O(n log n) complexity
	vs O(n^2) for naive digit-by-digit conversion.

	* src/arbint_gcd.c: Add arbint_xgcd (extended GCD with Bezout
	coefficients). Computes g = gcd(a, b) and coefficients x, y such
	that a*x + b*y = g. Any of g, x, y may be NULL if not needed.
	GMP-compatible semantics: when only g and x are requested, computes
	x = a^(-1) mod b for coprime inputs. Full aliasing support with
	"last write wins" semantics for output parameters.

	* src/arbint_gcd.c: Add Lehmer GCD algorithm for large operands
	(>= 32 limbs). Reduces multi-limb GCD to a sequence of single-limb
	matrix multiplications by extracting top bits into machine words.
	Asymptotically faster than binary GCD for large operands while
	maintaining numerical stability through careful quotient bounds.
	Automatically selected based on operand size.

	* src/arbint_gcd.c: Add modular inverse functions:
	- arbint_inv_mod: compute a^(-1) mod m via extended GCD.
	- arbint_inv_mod_u32: 32-bit modulus variant.

	* src/arbint_combin.c: New file. Implement combinatorial functions:
	arbint_fac_u32 (factorial), arbint_bin_u32u32 (binomial coefficient),
	arbint_fib_u32 (Fibonacci), arbint_lucas_u32 (Lucas numbers).
	Factorial uses binary splitting for O(n log^2 n) complexity.
	Binomial uses multiplicative formula with GCD reduction.
	Fibonacci/Lucas use fast doubling formulas for O(log n) complexity.

	* src/arbint_combin.c: Add arbint_is_power (perfect power detection).
	Determines if |a| = b^k for some integer b and k >= 2. Returns
	1 if a perfect power exists, 0 otherwise. Uses
	static table of 97 primes (up to 521) for small exponents, with
	dynamically cached sieve for larger prime exponents. Handles edge
	cases: 0 and +/-1 specially, even exponents forbidden for negative
	inputs. GMP-compatible interface.

	* src/arbint_combin.c: Add number-theoretic functions:
	- arbint_moebius: Mobius function via trial division for small
	  factors, returns -1/0/+1 based on square-free factorization.
	- arbint_totient: Euler's totient using product formula
	  phi(n) = n * prod(1 - 1/p) for prime factors p.
	- arbint_primorial: product of all primes <= n.
	- arbint_jacobi: Jacobi symbol using quadratic reciprocity and
	  supplementary laws for (-1/n) and (2/n).
	- arbint_legendre: Legendre symbol as special case of Jacobi.
	- arbint_kronecker: Kronecker symbol extending Jacobi to all
	  integer arguments.

	* src/arbint_combin.c: Add primality testing and generation:
	- arbint_isprime: Miller-Rabin test with configurable rounds.
	- arbint_nextprime: incremental search with wheel optimization.
	- arbint_prevprime: decremental search for largest prime < n.
	- arbint_removefactor_u32: extract all powers of a 32-bit factor,
	  returning the remaining cofactor and exponent count.

	* src/arbint_mul.c: Implement arbint_root() for computing integer
	k-th roots via Newton's method. Generalizes arbint_isqrt() to
	arbitrary positive integer exponents. Quadratic convergence with
	initial guess from bit count. Edge cases: k=0 returns EDOM, k=1
	returns input, k=2 delegates to arbint_isqrt. Supports aliasing.

	* src/arbint_mul_generic.c, src/arbint_mul_bmi2.c: Add fast
	truncated division by 3 (arbint_tdiv_q_3) using fixed Barrett
	constants. Used internally by arbint_root for the Newton iteration
	t = floor(((k-1)*x + a/x^(k-1)) / k) when k=3.

	* src/arbint_base.c: Add arbint_drop_caches to explicitly release
	global runtime caches (NTT roots of unity, prime sieve, etc.).
	Safe to call repeatedly; useful before memory debugging.

	* tests/test_str.c: New file. String conversion tests covering
	parsing and formatting in all supported bases, edge cases (zero,
	negative, leading zeros), large numbers, round-trip verification.

	* tests/test_xgcd.c: New file. Comprehensive tests for arbint_xgcd:
	basic Bezout identity verification, coprime pairs, non-coprime
	pairs, zero inputs, negative inputs, aliasing scenarios (g==a,
	x==b, all outputs same), Fibonacci pairs (worst case), large
	primes, highly composite numbers, and stochastic verification.

	* tests/test_is_power.c: New file. Comprehensive tests for
	arbint_is_power: small perfect powers (squares through 7th powers),
	negative powers (odd exponents only), composite exponent detection,
	near-miss values, semiprimes and non-powers, large base/small
	exponent, prime base powers, static table boundaries (exponent 521),
	dynamic sieve tests (exponents 523, 541, 2003, 3001).

	* tests/test_root.c: New file. Comprehensive tests for arbint_root:
	edge cases, perfect powers, non-perfect powers (floor behavior),
	k=2 delegation cross-verification, aliasing, large multi-limb
	operands, power/root round-trip, consecutive values, boundary
	values around perfect powers, and stochastic verification.

	* tests/test_combin.c: New file. Tests for combinatorial functions
	covering known values, edge cases, large inputs, and identities.

	* tests/test_numtheory.c: New file. Number-theoretic function
	tests covering Jacobi/Legendre/Kronecker symbols, Mobius function,
	Euler totient, primality testing, and prime generation.

	* tests/test_inv_mod.c: New file. Modular inverse tests covering
	coprime pairs, verification via a*inv = 1 (mod m), edge cases.

	* tests/test_removefactor.c: New file. Factor removal tests
	covering powers of small primes, composite factors, edge cases.

	* tests/test_framework.h: Add execution timing to test output.
	Tests now report elapsed time in seconds (e.g., "passed (0.154s)").

	* include/arbint.h: Add arbint_set_str, arbint_get_str, arbint_xgcd,
	arbint_is_power, arbint_root, arbint_fac_u32, arbint_bin_u32u32,
	arbint_fib_u32, arbint_lucas_u32, arbint_moebius, arbint_totient,
	arbint_primorial, arbint_jacobi, arbint_legendre, arbint_kronecker,
	arbint_isprime, arbint_nextprime, arbint_prevprime, arbint_inv_mod,
	arbint_inv_mod_u32, arbint_removefactor_u32, arbint_drop_caches
	to public API. Remove "unimplemented" comment block as all listed
	functions are now implemented.

2026-02-11  Kamila Szewczyk  <k@iczelia.net>

	* Version 0.0.3 released.

	* src/arbint_ntt.c, src/arbint_ntt.h: New files. Implement NTT
	(Number Theoretic Transform) multiplication using 3-prime CRT
	reconstruction with Goldilocks-family primes. O(n log n) complexity
	for very large operands (threshold: 1024 limbs).
	* src/arbint_ntt_core.inc: Shared NTT core included by all backends.
	Montgomery arithmetic, Cooley-Tukey butterflies, Garner CRT.
	* src/arbint_ntt_generic.c: Portable NTT using half-limb multiply.
	* src/arbint_ntt_bmi2.c: BMI2-optimized NTT using _mulx_u64.
	* src/arbint_ntt_avx2.c: AVX2+BMI2 NTT (foundation for future SIMD).

	* src/arbint_fdiv.c: New file. Implement floor division variants
	(arbint_fdiv_qr, arbint_fdiv_q, arbint_fdiv_r) with i32/u32 scalar
	variants. Quotient rounds toward negative infinity.
	* src/arbint_cdiv.c: New file. Implement ceiling division variants
	(arbint_cdiv_qr, arbint_cdiv_q, arbint_cdiv_r) with i32/u32 scalar
	variants. Quotient rounds toward positive infinity.

	* src/arbint_mul.c: Add fused multiply-accumulate operations
	(arbint_addmul, arbint_submul, arbint_addmul_u32, arbint_addmul_i32,
	arbint_submul_u32, arbint_submul_i32). Fused schoolbook loop for
	small operands avoids temporary allocation.
	* src/arbint_mul.c: Add modular exponentiation arbint_pow_u32u32_tmod
	with precomputed Barrett reduction for efficiency.

	* src/arbint_tdiv.c: Add divisibility testing (arbint_divisible,
	arbint_divisible_u32) with Barrett reduction for scalar divisors.
	Power-of-two divisibility checked in O(1) via trailing zero bits.
	* src/arbint_div.c: Add power-of-two division fast paths. Division
	by 2^k uses shifts/masks instead of full division algorithm. Applies
	to all division modes (truncated, floor, ceiling).

	* src/arbint_div.c, src/arbint_div.h: New files. Core multi-limb
	division (Knuth Algorithm D) factored out of arbint_tdiv.c.
	* src/arbint_div_generic.c: New file. Portable Knuth Algorithm D.
	* src/arbint_div_bmi2.c: New file. BMI2-optimized Knuth Algorithm D.

	* src/arbint_mul_generic.c, src/arbint_mul_bmi2.c: Add Toom-3
	squaring path to multiplication core.
	* src/arbint_mul.h: Retune thresholds based on benchmarking:
	Karatsuba mul 15 (was 32), Toom-3 mul 20 (was 96), Karatsuba sqr 10
	(was 24), Toom-3 sqr 18 (was 80). Add NTT threshold (1024 limbs).

	* tools/tune_thresholds.c: Use arbint_urandomb for random operand
	generation instead of deterministic squaring. Read threshold values
	from arbint_mul.h via stringify macros. Add --ntt flag for NTT
	threshold tuning with sizes 128-8192 limbs.
	* Makefile.am: tools/ no longer built by default; use 'make tools'.

	* src/platform-objects.txt: Data-driven platform-specific object
	management. Generator in bootstrap produces Makefile.platform-rules.am
	with conditional LIBADD and dependency tracking rules.

	* tests/test_ntt.c: New file. NTT multiplication tests covering
	threshold boundaries, power-of-two sizes, unbalanced operands,
	algebraic identities, and stochastic verification.
	* tests/test_mul.c: Fix 32-bit platform compatibility (avoid shift
	by limb width).

	* src/arbint_gcd.c, src/arbint_gcd.h: New files. Implement GCD and LCM
	(arbint_gcd, arbint_lcm, arbint_gcd_u32, arbint_lcm_u32). Binary GCD
	(Stein's algorithm) for large operands (> 4 limbs), Euclidean algorithm
	with modular reduction for size-disparate operands. Result always
	non-negative; operates on magnitudes (signs ignored).
	* tests/test_gcd.c: New file. Comprehensive GCD/LCM tests covering
	basic cases, zeros, negative inputs, aliasing, symmetry, multi-limb
	operands, Fibonacci pairs (worst-case), scaling property, threshold
	boundaries, and stochastic verification.

	* include/arbint.h: Add ~28 new API functions for division variants,
	fused multiply-accumulate, divisibility testing, modular exponentiation,
	GCD/LCM.

2026-02-10  Kamila Szewczyk  <k@iczelia.net>

	* Version 0.0.2 released.

	* src/Makefile.am: Add Emscripten/WebAssembly build support.  On
	emscripten, bypass libtool's broken link mode via convenience library
	(noinst_LTLIBRARIES) + direct emcc -sSIDE_MODULE link.  Replace
	EXTRA_*_SOURCES with EXTRA_DIST to avoid automake 1.18 phantom rule
	generation bug that caused platform-specific files to be compiled
	without required flags (e.g. -mbmi2).
	* tests/Makefile.am: Conditional LDADD for emscripten (link against
	libarbint.wasm instead of libarbint.la).  Add LOG_COMPILER +
	AM_LOG_FLAGS for running wasm tests via run_wasm_test.sh under node.
	* tests/run_wasm_test.sh: New test runner for emscripten.  Finds JS
	output from emcc, copies side module next to test binary, executes
	under node.
	* configure.ac: Force enable_shared=yes on emscripten when libtool's
	ld_shlibs detection fails.  Add ARBINT_HOST_EMSCRIPTEN conditional.
	Add ARBINT_EMSCRIPTEN_TEST_LDFLAGS for -sMAIN_MODULE=2 -sNODERAWFS.
	Skip arc4random_buf on emscripten (links but declaration missing).
	* .github/workflows/ci.yml: Add build-wasm job with wasm32/wasm64
	matrix (with and without LTO).  Node 24 for wasm64 Memory64 support.
	Wasm artifacts included in repack-artifacts job.
	* src/arbint_random_getentropy.c: Emscripten entropy via getentropy()
	(routes to crypto.getRandomValues).

	* src/arbint_random.c, src/arbint_random.h: Implement Mersenne Twister
	(MT19937) PRNG with platform entropy seeding. Add arbint_urandomb and
	arbint_urandomm with rejection sampling for uniform distribution.
	* src/arbint_random_urandom.c: /dev/urandom entropy source (Linux/POSIX).
	* src/arbint_random_arc4.c: arc4random_buf entropy source (macOS/BSD).
	* src/arbint_random_winapi.c: BCryptGenRandom/CryptGenRandom entropy
	source (Windows).

	* src/arbint_hash.c, src/arbint_hash.h: Implement cryptographic hashing
	(arbint_hash_slow via SHA-256, arbint_hash_fast via CRC32C) with
	counter-mode construction for variable-length output.
	* src/arbint_hash_generic.c: Portable SHA-256 and CRC32C implementations.
	* src/arbint_hash_shani.c: SHA-NI hardware-accelerated SHA-256 (x86).
	* src/arbint_hash_crc32c_sse42.c: SSE4.2 hardware-accelerated CRC32C (x86-64).
	* src/arbint_hash_crc32c_neon.c: ARM CRC32+PMULL hardware-accelerated
	CRC32C (AArch64).
	* src/arbint_hash_sha2_neon.c: ARM SHA-2 crypto extension SHA-256 (AArch64).

	* src/arbint_bitops.c, src/arbint_bitops.h: Implement two's-complement
	bitwise operations (and, or, xor, not), bit queries (testbit, setbit,
	clrbit), counting functions (popcount, hammingdist, ctz, clz), and
	size queries (nbits, sizeinbase).
	* src/arbint_bitops_popcnt.c: x86 POPCNT-accelerated population count.

	* src/arbint_shift.c, src/arbint_shift.h: Implement left and right shift
	operations (arbint_shl, arbint_shr) with limb+bit decomposition.

	* src/arbint_mul.c: Add arbint_pow_u32 (binary exponentiation) and
	arbint_isqrt (Newton's method). Dedicated squaring paths with
	Karatsuba optimization.
	* src/arbint_mul_core.inc: Shared schoolbook/Karatsuba/Toom-Cook 3-way
	multiplication and squaring template, included by both generic and BMI2
	backends. Toom-3 threshold at 96 limbs.

	* src/arbint_tdiv_generic.c: Implement Knuth Algorithm D for multi-limb
	division, replacing the O(n^2*bits) binary algorithm with O(n*m).
	* src/arbint_tdiv_bmi2.c: BMI2-optimized Knuth Algorithm D variant.

	* configure.ac: Add AArch64 host detection. Add feature detection for
	POPCNT, SHA-NI, SSE4.2 CRC32C, ARM CRC32, ARM PMULL, ARM SHA-2.
	Add --disable-entropy option. Detect explicit_bzero/memset_s.
	Raise default optimization from -O2 to -O3. Enable
	-fno-semantic-interposition where supported.
	* m4/arbint_arm_feature_check.m4: New macro for ARM feature detection.

	* include/arbint.h: Add ~19 new implemented API functions and declare
	stubs for number-theoretic functions (moebius, totient, carmichael,
	isprime, inv_mod, is_square, is_power, root).
	* src/arbint_cpu.c, src/arbint_cpu.h: AArch64 runtime feature detection
	via getauxval.

	* tests/: Add test_random, test_hash, test_shift, test_bitops, test_pow,
	test_isqrt, test_sqr, test_mul_exhaustive, compute_e, compute_bitops.
	* man/c-arbint.3.in: Document all new APIs.
	* contrib/sign_release: Armored signatures, bundled archive output.
	* README => README.md: Convert to Markdown.

